{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 129, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Upgrading edge 0 to 3x3 conv gives much smaller gains when the direct 0->3 edge is a pooling op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a removed direct input-output edge with a skip restores connectivity, giving a large gain."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a strong 3x3 conv on the direct edge costs more than removing a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 1 is disconnected so upgrading edge 4 yields almost no gain."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "A pooling direct edge reduces the benefit of upgrading edge 5 to 3x3 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "A pooling direct edge reduces the benefit of upgrading edge 4 to 3x3 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with pooling loses capacity, whereas replacing weaker ops is roughly neutral or positive."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with a skip removes learned capacity, unlike replacing none or 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on edge 0 costs far more than deleting a 1x1 conv, skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_